== FINDINGS (observations for the lead; not FAIL bases)
- O1: TestWS1ExpectedReturnDataAttribute uses strings.Contains over each whole rendered template.
  - It pins the attribute's VALUE, not which element carries it.
  - Today each template has exactly one data-expected-return (grep), so this is equivalent.
  - Moving the attribute to a sibling element would survive go+node. Only oracle E8b binds the attribute to the display node.
- O2: the new C1k node test asserts the displays' textContent, not the QA range's aria-valuetext. The aria is derived from the same text in the same function, and the ruling did not require an aria check.
- O3: the new test's in-card sentinel "6.2" is a plausible real figure.
  - The in-card-only self-check relies on the fake DOM's recompute (5.8) differing from it.
  - The pre-existing C1/P5 test (sentinel 9.9) independently kills in-card recompute (C1m: "expected ... (9.9) verbatim").
